.TH ZFSWATCHER 8 "2026-11-22" "version 0.8.0"
.SH NAME
zfswatcher \- ZFS pool monitoring and notification daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zfswatcher
.RB [\| \-c
.IR config-file \|]
.RB [\| \-d \|]
.RB [\| \-P \|]
.RB [\| \-T \|]
.RB [\| \-\-test\-notify \|]
.RB [\| \-t \|]
.RB [\| \-v \|]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B zfswatcher
daemon periodically checks the ZFS pool status and sends notifications
about any changes. It also optionally controls the disk enclosure LEDs
and provides a web interface for viewing the ZFS status and logs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-conf " \fIconfig-file\fR"
Use an alternate
.I config-file
instead of the default
.IR /etc/zfs/zfswatcher.conf .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug mode which outputs all messages to STDOUT.
Internal diagnostic messages (written to STDERR, under systemd to the
journal, see
.BR journalctl (1))
then include the debug level.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-passwordhash
Read a password and print its bcrypt hash (cost 10) for the
.B password
setting of a
.B wwwuser
section in the configuration file. On a terminal the password is read
without echo and asked for twice; otherwise one line is read from standard
input, so the option can be used in scripts. Hashes in the older MD5 crypt
format ("$1$...") are still accepted in the configuration but are deprecated.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-generate\-token
Generate a new API token (the string "zfsw_" followed by 43 random
characters) and print it once, together with the line
.B hash = sha256:\fI...\fR
for an
.B apitoken
section of the configuration file. Only the hash is stored in the
configuration, so the token must be saved immediately. See
.B CONFIGURATION
below.
.TP
.B \-\-test\-notify
Send one test message to all enabled outputs (log files, syslog, e-mail,
webhooks) and exit; the daemon is not started. The message has the severity
.BR emerg ,
so it passes every
.B level
setting. The exit status is 1 if a webhook delivery fails (the other outputs
are best effort) or an output cannot be set up.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Test the configuration file syntax and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Besides the options described in the configuration file comments, a few
settings control the web interface.
.TP
.B refresh
In section
.BR [www] :
the interval in seconds (2 to 3600) at which the dashboard and the pool
status pages reload their content in the browser (using htmx). The default
is 10,
.B 0
switches the refresh off. The pages work without JavaScript, they just do
not update. Any other value is a configuration error.
.TP
.BR severitycssclassmap ", " poolstatecssclassmap ", " devstatecssclassmap ", " usedstatecssclassmap
In section
.BR [www] :
CSS classes of the Bootstrap 5 based pages. The class names of the former
Bootstrap 3 pages (for example
.BR text\-error ,
.BR progress\-bar\-warning
or
.B error
for log lines) are still accepted and translated when the configuration is
loaded.
.TP
.B role
In a
.B wwwuser
or
.B apitoken
section: one of
.BR viewer ,
.B operator
or
.BR admin .
A viewer may see the dashboard, pool status, usage, statistics, enclosure
and about pages. An operator may additionally see the logs and switch the
locate LEDs. An admin may do everything (currently the same as an operator).
Without
.B role
the user is an admin. An invalid value is a configuration error.
.TP
.B apitoken
Section
.RB [ apitoken
.IR \(dqname\(dq ]
with
.BR enable ,
.B hash
and
.BR role .
The hash has the form
.B sha256:\fI64 hexadecimal digits\fR
and is produced by
.BR "zfswatcher \-T" .
A client sends the token as
.B Authorization: Bearer
.IR token .
Tokens are accepted only for paths below
.IR <rootdir>/api/ ;
for all other pages only HTTP Basic authentication of a
.B wwwuser
works. Basic authentication is accepted for the API as well.
.TP
.B webhook
Section
.RB [ webhook
.IR \(dqname\(dq ]
with
.BR enable ,
.BR level ,
.BR url ,
.BR preset ,
.B token
and
.BR throttle .
All messages of one check run are sent in one HTTP POST request to
.BR url ,
which must start with http:// or https://. The
.B preset
is
.B generic
(JSON with host, severity, title and a list of messages; the default),
.BR ntfy ,
.BR gotify ,
.B discord
or
.BR slack .
The
.B token
is sent as
.B Authorization: Bearer
(generic, ntfy) or as
.B X-Gotify-Key
(gotify).
.B throttle
is the minimum number of seconds between two requests. Attachments are not
sent. A request times out after 10 seconds and is repeated once after a
network error or an HTTP 5xx status. Errors are written to the diagnostics
(stderr, journal), never the token or the query string of the URL. An invalid
.B url
or
.B preset
is a configuration error.
.SH JSON API
A read only JSON API is available below
.IR <rootdir>/api/v1/ :
.BR info ", " pools ", " pools/ \fIname\fR ", " usage
(role viewer) and
.B events
(role operator). Only GET and HEAD are supported. See the section "JSON API"
in README.md; the API may change until version 1.0.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload configuration and reopen logs.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Terminate gracefully.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The daemon exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/zfs/zfswatcher.conf
Default configuration file.
.SH NOTES
The
.B zfswatcher
process does not "daemonize" itself (fork or double-fork to become a
background process) like most traditional Unix daemons do. This is a
modern approach and allows system process management daemons such as
.BR upstart (8)
and
.BR systemd (8)
to keep better control of the service. This can be worked around by
using a tool such as 
.BR start-stop-daemon (8).
.PP
Currently an external utility called
.B ledctl
which is part of the
.B ledmon
package is required for enclosure LED control.
